{
  "requirement": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.validation.criterion_trait`\n\n`Criterion::source_node_id` identifies the criterion's\n{term}`requirements.sdk.graph.validation.source_node`:\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Criterion<D: Domain>: Send + Sized {\n    // ...\n\n    /// The node this question is about.\n    fn source_node_id(&self) -> D::NodeId;\n\n    // ...\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement has one obligation. `Criterion::source_node_id` must return the criterion's source node, which is the node the criterion is evaluated on. Two marked tests cover it.\n\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested]` builds a `Review` criterion whose `source_node_id` returns its `source` field (checked in `impl[Review<O>/Criterion<Application>]/fn[source_node_id]`). It runs `validator.verify` and asserts that `value.source_node_id()` equals `&Node(1)`. After storing and loading the evidence, it asserts that `loaded.source_node_id()` equals `value.source_node_id()`. This shows the trait method's result is what reaches the validated record.\n- `src/authoring/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[review_graph_persists_and_reuses_a_negative_validation_through_the_sdk]` calls the trait method directly with `assert_eq!(review().source_node_id(), node)`. This checks that the SDK `Review` criterion returns the node it was built for. That node is a non-trivial `HabeasNode::Requirement` value, and the test also uses it to locate the evidence path.\n\nBoth tests exercise the method on real criterion implementations and assert the expected identity. Together they cover a test-domain criterion and the production SDK criterion. The requirement names no other boundary or failure case, so I found no gap.",
